## Why (framework evidence, `doc/plan/c016-worklog/review-layer-ownership-audit.md` §4 and §11 item 2)
The .NET ClientServer client (`ZLinkClientServerClientRuntime.cs`, `ReconnectAsync`) reported that after `disconnect(endpoint)` the
terminal monitor edge (Disconnected/Closed) did not progress for ~5 s unless the application kept polling the socket, so the
framework created a SECOND POLLIN poller on the same socket to drive Core command progress (round-2 trace in
`bucketF-dotnet-clientserver-readmit-2-summary.md`). If Core requires an application poll for its own disconnect command to
progress, that is a polling §3 lost-wake/progress violation; if it does not, the framework poller is a workaround to delete.

## What to do (public C API contract tests, tcp + inproc)
1. DEALER connected+admitted to a ROUTER endpoint; the application registers the DEALER on a public poller but (a) is blocked
   in `zlink_poller_wait`, (b) is NOT waiting at all (idle). Server closes/`disconnect`s the pipe → assert the Disconnected monitor
   event and the automatic reconnect READY arrive within a bounded time in both cases without any application poll.
2. Application calls `zlink_disconnect(endpoint)` then immediately `zlink_connect(endpoint)` on the same socket (before the
   terminal edge) → assert the Disconnected/Closed edge of the old pipe arrives, the new pipe becomes READY, and a REQUEST
   submitted right after `connect` is queued on the NEW pipe (its reply arrives), never on the retiring one. Measure the time
   between `disconnect()` return and the terminal edge with no application poll.
3. If any case stalls (edge only after an application poll, or the request lands on the retiring pipe): root-cause in
   `core/src/**` (command mailbox processing / reaper / connecter reconnect path), fix minimally, keep the tests as the
   regression; full `ctest -j2` in the worktree + §5 checks + hotpath policy check if `scripts/` provides one.
   If everything progresses per spec: say so with the measured bounds (that authorises deleting the framework's second poller).
4. Deliverable: `doc/plan/c016-worklog/core-disconnect-progress-summary.md` in the MAIN tree: results table (case × transport
   × with/without poll × elapsed ms), cause + diff summary if fixed, test names, gate counts, BLOCKERS. Leave the diff
   uncommitted in the worktree.
